Tue Oct 27 19:23:36 UTC 2026 - Matej Cepl <mcepl@cepl.eu>

- Update to 0.2.0:
  - Features
    - gt pr merge can mark a pull request as manually merged with
      --commit SHA.
    - gt repo edit adds --allow-manual-merge and
      --autodetect-manual-merge.
    - gt run logs --tail N prints only the last N lines of each
      job's log, also with --failed.
    - gt run watch --expect-head fails before waiting when the
      run is for another commit.
  - Enhancements
    - gt run watch and gt workflow run --follow exit with 5 when
      the run completes without success, so a red build can be
      told apart from a failure of gt itself (still 1), and with
      6 when --expect-head doesn't match.
    - gt pr edit, gt release edit and gt label edit open a form
      when no fields are given.
    - gt release create and gt repo create ask for release
      details and repository settings when run interactively.
      --project accepts project IDs.
    - Every required prompt is marked as required.
  - Fixes
    - gt release create in a clone refuses to tag a different
      commit than the local one. It resolves --target HEAD and
      short SHAs to the local commit and, without --target, only
      creates a new tag when HEAD is the head of the default
      branch.
    - The remote preference in config.yml is tried first, and gt
      falls back to another remote when it is missing or points
      elsewhere. --remote stays strict.
    - Projects owned by the repository's user are found.
    - gt pr create seeds the form with the pull request template
      of the chosen base branch.
    - gt pr view keeps a request for changes in the reviewers
      when there are later comments.
    - gt pr list lists no pull requests in a repository without
      commits, instead of failing.
    - gt browse takes the SHA from --commit SHA written with a
      space.
    - The error for a GITEA_TOKEN without an instance names the
      variables it needs.
  - Documentation
    - Install with Homebrew.
    - New agent skill for gt.
- Add provided skills to %%{_datadir}/skills/gt

